                  <msItem>
                     <title>'Matheus glo minori glo cum B'</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">2o fo.: 'liber'. This is a 'bad' lectio
                        probatoria being in fact the first word of the text. Cf. Canterbury
                        Cathedral 34 which was marked at first 'Matheus glo minori glo cum B', but
                        altered to 'Matheus glo cum C'. The original inscription is in the same hand
                        as that here.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Apparently a foreign manuscript, but notes are
                        in English medieval hands.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
